# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk J (Scentless to Spur Mount). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Scentless": "You touch a willing creature or an object that nobody is wearing or carrying. For 1 hour the target gives off no scent. Creatures that rely on smell have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to find the target and on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track it. A creature that senses its surroundings only by smell cannot see the target at all. The spell does nothing against targets with an unusually strong odor, such as a ghast.",
"Screaming Ray": "You loose a ray of psychic energy at a creature within 30 feet. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d4 Psychic damage and is Deafened until the end of your next turn. If the target succeeds on a Constitution save it is not Deafened. **At Higher Levels.** You create one extra ray for each slot level above 1st. You can aim the rays at one target or split them among several.",
"Scribe": "You copy a one-page written work by laying a blank sheet of paper or parchment near it. Every word, picture and mark is reproduced in your own handwriting or drawing style. The blank sheet must be large enough to hold the original. Magical properties are not copied, so this cannot duplicate spell scrolls or magic books.",
"Scry Ambush": "You sense an enemy's strike an instant before it comes. As a reaction, when a foe is about to start an attack, you cast this spell. A number of allies equal to your spellcasting ability modifier (minimum 1) plus your proficiency bonus are not surprised. If you yourself were surprised, you must make a spellcasting check when your reaction would trigger, with a DC equal to the current initiative count. On a failure you stay surprised and cannot use your reaction to cast this spell until after your next turn. On a success you can cast it right away as a reaction.",
"Sculpt Snow": "While standing in an area full of snow, you shape it into one Large object, two Medium objects, or four smaller ones within 60 feet. Cast as an action, the shapes are only crude likenesses of generic creatures or objects. Cast over 1 minute, they look more realistic and can vaguely resemble specific creatures, enough to be recognized but not enough to fool anyone. The sculptures are as sturdy as a snowman. You can animate them with animate objects or similar magic, and they gain the stats that spell provides. Their attacks deal normal damage plus a similar amount of Cold damage. A Medium sculpture, for example, deals 2d6 + 1 Bludgeoning plus 2d6 + 1 Cold. **At Higher Levels.** You can sculpt one extra Large object for each slot level above 2nd. Two Large objects can be replaced by one Huge object.",
"Seal of Sanctuary": "Casting takes 1 minute and consumes incense and special inks worth 250 gp. You inscribe an angelic seal on the ground, a floor, or another solid surface. It creates a sphere of sanctuary with a 50-foot radius centered on the seal and lasts 24 hours. Aberrations, elementals, fey, fiends and undead that come within 5 feet of the boundary sense a deadly barrier ahead. A creature of those types that touches or tries to cross the boundary by any means, including teleportation or extradimensional travel, makes a Charisma save. On a failure it takes 10d8 Radiant damage, is pushed to 5 feet outside the boundary, and cannot target anything inside with attacks, spells or abilities until the spell ends. On a success it takes half damage and can cross. A fiend away from its home plane is destroyed outright with no save. Aberrations, elementals, fey and undead already inside have Disadvantage on ability checks, attack rolls and saving throws, and each takes 2d8 Radiant damage at the start of its turn. Other creatures inside cannot be Charmed or Frightened. The seal has AC 18, 50 hit points, resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage, and immunity to Psychic and Poison damage. Ranged attacks against it have Disadvantage. If the surface it is drawn on is destroyed, the seal stays in place, even hanging in midair. The spell ends only when the seal drops to 0 hit points.",
"Searing Sun": "You must be able to see the sun. You intensify its light and heat over a cylinder with a 50-foot radius and 200-foot height, centered on a point within 200 feet. Each creature that starts its turn in the area takes 5d8 Fire damage, or half on a successful Constitution save. A creature shaded by a solid object such as an awning, a building or a boulder has Advantage on the save. Concentration, up to 1 minute. On your turn you can use an action to move the cylinder's center up to 20 feet along the ground.",
"See Beyond": "You touch a willing creature. For 1 hour (Concentration) it can see through anything that blocks sight, including objects, creatures, spells and effects, out to 30 feet. Within that distance it freely chooses what appears opaque and what appears transparent. Seeing a target does not remove other requirements for attacking or casting at it. A foe with total cover can be seen but not shot with an arrow, since the cover still blocks the shot. A spell like geas, which needs only a visible target, can still affect that foe.",
"Seed of Destruction": "You plant a growing five-headed hydra in a living creature you can see within 60 feet. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the embryo takes hold and matures in 1d3 + 1 rounds. At the start of each of its turns while it gestates, the target takes 5d4 Slashing damage, or half on a successful Constitution save. When the time is up, a tiny hydra bursts from the target at the start of your turn, appears in an unoccupied space next to it, and instantly grows into a Huge aberration. Nearby creatures are pushed away to make room. It is a standard hydra that can also cast bane as an action (save DC 11) with no components. It rolls its own initiative and obeys your spoken commands without costing you an action. With no command, it attacks the nearest living creature. At the end of each of its turns, you make a DC 15 Charisma save. On a success it stays under your control and friendly. On a failure it turns hostile to everyone and attacks the nearest creature. The hydra vanishes after 1 hour or when wish or similar magic ends it. Before it matures, the embryo can be destroyed with dispel magic under the normal rules for high-level magic.",
"Seeping Death": "Make a melee spell attack against a creature within reach. On a hit, the target's Dexterity score is reduced by 1d4 and it contracts the seeping death disease for 3 days. As a natural disease, it can be removed early by any effect that cures disease. **Seeping Death.** A necrotic pestilence slowly liquefies the victim's flesh. At the end of each long rest, the diseased creature makes a Constitution save. On a failure its Dexterity score drops by 1d4 again. The reduction lasts until it finishes a long rest after being cured. If Dexterity falls to 0, the creature dies.",
"Seer's Reaction": "Your foreknowledge lets you act first. As a reaction at the start of another creature's turn, you roll a new initiative with a +5 bonus. If the result beats your current initiative, your place in the order changes. If it also beats the current point in the order, you take your next turn immediately and use the higher number from the next round on.",
"Seer's reaction": "Your foreknowledge lets you act first. As a reaction at the start of another creature's turn, you reroll your Dexterity check for initiative with a +5 bonus. Your initiative becomes the higher of the two results. If that number is higher than the current initiative count, you take your turn immediately and switch to the higher number next round.",
"Semblance of Dread": "You take on the dreadful face of the faceless god Nyarlathotep for 1 minute (Concentration). A creature within 10 feet that can see you cannot willingly move closer unless it succeeds on a Wisdom save as it tries to approach. A creature can attempt only one such save per turn. Constructs and undead are immune. While the spell lasts you have vulnerability to Radiant damage and Advantage on saving throws against effects that cause the Frightened condition.",
"Servant of Doom": "As a bonus action you draw on a force of destruction for 1 minute (Concentration). Each time you cast it, choose one form. **Emissary.** Your blood glows through your skin and extra eyes open on your flesh. You gain a flying speed equal to your walking speed and can hover, but you must stay within 5 feet of the ground. You gain truesight out to 60 feet. Creatures have Disadvantage on Wisdom saves against your spells and abilities. You have Advantage on attack rolls based on Intelligence or Wisdom. **Envoy.** Your skin turns stonelike and bony growths cover your body. You ignore difficult terrain. You can move through walls and other solid barriers if you succeed on a Strength check made just before moving into the barrier, with a DC of 10 plus twice the barrier's thickness in feet. You have Advantage on attack rolls based on Strength or Dexterity. Your melee weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 Slashing damage on a hit.",
"Shade": "A magical screen covers your eyes for 10 minutes (Concentration). While it lasts you are immune to blindness caused by visible effects, such as color spray. It does not cure blindness you already have. Any penalties you normally take on attacks or ability checks in sunlight do not apply. **At Higher Levels.** The duration rises by 10 minutes for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Shadow Armor": "You draw on the Plane of Shadow to shield yourself. As a reaction when you are targeted by an attack, before the roll, shadows bend around you. The attack is made with Disadvantage, and you have resistance to Radiant damage until the start of your next turn.",
"Shadow Bite": "You jab a needle of cold, sharp pain into a creature within 60 feet. The target makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 Necrotic damage and has its speed halved until the start of your next turn. The damage becomes 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at level 11 and 4d6 at level 17.",
"Shadow Blindness": "Make a melee spell attack against a creature you touch that has innate darkvision. On a hit its darkvision is negated for 1 round, after which it returns. The spell does not affect darkvision that comes from a spell or magic item. The target keeps all its other senses.",
"Shadow Gateway": "Casting takes 10 minutes. You draw a circle of black chalk up to 15 feet across within 30 feet and chant for the full casting time, opening a portal to the Plane of Shadow. It fills the circle as a swirl of inky darkness that cannot be seen through. Anything passing through arrives safely. The portal stays open for 1 minute or until you stop concentrating, and can be used in both directions as often as you like while it is open.",
"Shadow Hands": "A freezing blast of shadow bursts from you in a 10-foot cone. Each creature in it takes 2d4 Necrotic damage and is Frightened until the end of its next turn. A successful Wisdom save halves the damage and negates the Frightened condition. **At Higher Levels.** The damage rises by 2d4 for each slot level above 1st.",
"Shadow Metamorphosis": "You touch a creature of Huge size or smaller, or one object no more than 20 feet in any dimension, and turn it into malleable shadow-stuff for 1 minute (Concentration). An affected object is still solid but easy to shape or compress. A locked door could not be walked through, but could be pulled aside like a curtain or lifted like a tent flap and crawled under. An unwilling creature makes a Constitution save to avoid the effect. An affected creature is amorphous and can pass through a space as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing. In dim light or darkness it has Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. It cannot attack or cast spells and has vulnerability to Radiant damage.",
"Shadow Monsters": "Choose up to two creatures within 120 feet. Each makes a Wisdom save. On a failure the creature sees its allies as hostile shadowy monsters and must attack its nearest ally. An affected creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Concentration, up to 1 minute. **At Higher Levels.** You can target one extra creature for each slot level above 4th.",
"Shadow Puppets": "You animate the shadow of a creature within 60 feet so that it attacks its owner. As a bonus action when you cast the spell, or as an action on later turns while you concentrate (up to 1 minute), make a melee spell attack against the creature. On a hit it takes 2d8 Psychic damage and must succeed on an Intelligence save or be Incapacitated until the start of your next turn.",
"Shadow Step": "You can open a short-lived portal between two dark areas. While you concentrate (up to 1 minute), if you begin your turn in dim light or darkness, you can open a portal to another area of dim light or darkness within 60 feet and move there. Doing so uses all your movement for the turn, whatever the distance. You can use it while Prone. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks.",
"Shadow Tendrils": "Ribbons of dark, half-real force stretch from your hand within 30 feet for 1 minute (Concentration). As an action you can make a melee spell attack with them against a creature in range. On a hit the target takes 2d8 Cold damage and must succeed on a Dexterity save or be Restrained. A creature that starts its turn Restrained by the tendrils takes the Cold damage again. It can use an action to make a Dexterity check against your spell save DC to break free. As a bonus action on your turn, you can drag a Restrained creature up to 15 feet toward you. The tendrils have AC 13 and 12 hit points. They are immune to Bludgeoning damage and to Piercing and Slashing from nonmagical weapons, and vulnerable to Radiant damage. If they are destroyed while the spell is active, you can re-form them as a bonus action on your turn.",
"Shadow Trove": "Casting takes 1 minute. You paint a door about 2 feet square on a hard surface, creating a portal into the void. It peels off the surface and floats within 5 feet of you, following as you move, and breathes out an icy chill. It lasts 1 hour. You can store up to 750 pounds of nonliving matter in it, held in the frozen void until you take it out. Anything still inside when the spell ends is lost. You can name a number of creatures up to your Intelligence modifier who share access. Only you and they can put objects in. **At Higher Levels.** The duration rises by 2 hours for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Shadows Brought to Light": "You can cast this spell only as a ritual, taking 10 minutes. Choose a creature within 30 feet. It makes a Charisma save. On a failure its shadow comes to life and reveals one of the creature's most embarrassing secrets, something it would not want widely known (the GM chooses). You decide whether everyone present hears it, spoken in a twisted copy of the target's voice, or whether the shadow whispers it only to you. It speaks in the target's native language. If the target has no scandalous secret or no spoken language, the spell fails as though the save had succeeded. If the secret was spoken aloud, the target takes a -2 penalty on Charisma checks involving anyone who heard it, lasting until you finish a long rest. **Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, the target has Disadvantage on those Charisma checks instead of the -2 penalty.",
"Shadowy Retribution": "You can cast this spell only as a ritual, taking 10 minutes. You fill a small silver cup with your own blood, taking 1d4 Piercing damage, while chanting dark curses. You drink it and swear an oath of vengeance against anyone who harms you. The oath lasts 12 hours. If you drop to 0 hit points during that time, a shadow appears within 5 feet of you. It attacks the creature that reduced you to 0 hit points and ignores all others until one of them dies, then fades away. **Group Spellcasting.** Each other spellcaster who helps you adds one more creature, up to 6 shadows in total. **Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, a banshee appears instead of a shadow. Extra creatures from group spellcasting are still shadows.",
"Shared Sacrifice": "Casting takes 1 minute. You and up to five allies within 60 feet pool part of your life force for 1 hour. Each target takes 5 Necrotic damage that cannot be reduced but can be healed normally, and those hit points go into a shared pool. As an action, any creature that contributed can touch another creature and draw from the pool to heal it. The creature heals hit points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier, and the pool shrinks by the same amount. This can repeat until the pool is empty or the spell ends.",
"Sheen of Ice": "A small icy globe flies from your finger to a point within 60 feet and bursts in a spray of ice. Each creature within 20 feet of that point makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it is coated in ice for 1 minute and moves at half speed. An invisible creature is outlined by the ice and loses the benefit of invisibility while coated. The effect ends on a creature that takes 5 or more Fire damage.",
"Shield of Star and Shadow": "You wrap yourself in a shroud of night sky, swirling shadow dotted with tiny lights. For 10 minutes you have resistance to either Radiant or Necrotic damage, chosen when you cast the spell, and you shed dim light in a 10-foot radius. You can end the spell early with an action.",
"Shield of Starlight": "You wrap yourself in a shroud of night sky, swirling shadow dotted with tiny lights. For 10 minutes you have resistance to either Radiant or Necrotic damage, chosen when you cast the spell, and you shed dim light in a 10-foot radius. You can end the spell early with an action.",
"Shifting the Odds": "You wrap yourself in strands of chaotic energy and gain Advantage on the next attack roll or ability check you make. Fate balances the books, though. The second attack roll or ability check you make after casting this spell, whichever comes first, has Disadvantage.",
"Shiver": "You fill a humanoid within 30 feet with such cold that its teeth chatter and its body shakes. Roll 5d8. The total is the highest number of hit points a creature can have and still be affected. The target makes a Constitution save. On a failure it cannot cast spells or load a missile weapon until the end of your next turn. A creature that has been affected is immune to this spell for 24 hours. The roll increases by 4d8 at level 5 (9d8), level 11 (13d8) and level 17 (17d8).",
"Shocking Shroud": "Arcs of electricity play over your body for 10 minutes. You have resistance to Lightning damage. Whenever a creature within 5 feet hits you with a melee attack, lightning strikes it for 2d8 Lightning damage. You can end the spell early with an action.",
"Shroud of Death": "A black veil of necrotic energy feeds on the living around you. Concentration, up to 10 rounds. When you cast it, every living creature you can see within 30 feet takes 1 Necrotic damage, and you gain that many hit points as temporary hit points. The amount rises to 2 per creature at the start of your second turn concentrating on the spell, 3 at the start of your third, and so on. Creatures within 30 feet that you can see at the start of each of your turns are affected. There is no save. A creature escapes by moving more than 30 feet away or out of your line of sight, and becomes vulnerable again if it returns. The temporary hit points last until the spell ends.",
"Sidestep Arrow": "As a reaction when an enemy makes a ranged attack or ranged spell attack against you, before it resolves, you can cast this spell. At least one other foe must be within 10 feet of you. You move up to 15 feet to a spot where an enemy stands between you and the attacker. If no such spot exists, the spell does nothing. You must be able to move, so you cannot be Restrained, Grappled or otherwise unable to move. This movement does not provoke opportunity attacks. The attack is then resolved against the intervening foe instead of you.",
"Sign of Koth": "Casting takes 1 round. You invoke the twilight citadels of Koth to create a field shaped like a 60-foot-radius, 60-foot-tall cylinder centered on you. Its only visible sign is a black rune on every door, window and other opening inside. The effect is permanent. Choose a creature type: aberration, beast, celestial, dragon, elemental, fey, fiend, giant, humanoid, monstrosity, ooze, plant or undead. Creatures of that type, you included if it applies, are affected as follows. They cannot willingly enter the area by nonmagical means, as if it were an invisible wall of force. If they try to enter by teleportation, a dimensional shortcut or other magic, they make a Charisma save or the attempt fails. They cannot hear sounds that start inside the cylinder. They have Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets inside. They cannot Charm, Frighten or possess creatures inside. Unaffected creatures that take a short rest inside regain twice the usual hit points for each Hit Die spent. When you cast the spell you can reverse it, so affected creatures cannot leave instead of cannot enter, cannot hear sounds from outside, and so on. In that case there is no short rest benefit. **At Higher Levels.** The radius grows by 30 feet for each slot level above 7th.",
"Silhouette": "You create a shadow play on a screen or wall of up to 100 square feet. A number of creatures equal to your Intelligence score can watch it. The figures make no sound but can dance, run, move, kiss, fight and more. Most are generic shapes such as a rabbit or a dwarf, but a number equal to your Intelligence modifier can resemble specific individuals. Concentration, up to 1 minute.",
"Sir Mittinz's Move Curse": "Casting takes 1 hour. When you are within 20 feet of a cursed creature or object, you can move the curse to a different creature or object that is also within 20 feet. A curse must go from object to object or from creature to creature.",
"Sleep of the Deep": "Your magic haunts the dreams of others with awful visions of the non-Euclidean city of R'lyeh. Choose a sleeping creature within 60 feet that you know is there. Creatures that do not sleep, such as elves, cannot be targeted. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it gains no benefit from that rest, and when it wakes it gains one level of Exhaustion and suffers short-term madness. The effect lasts up to 8 hours. **At Higher Levels.** You can target one extra creature for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Slippery Fingers": "As a bonus action you set small events in motion against a creature within 30 feet. Unless it succeeds on a Charisma save, it drops one nonmagical item you choose that it is holding. The spell cannot make a creature drop a magic item.",
"Slither": "You briefly become a shadow, a humanoid-shaped absence of light and not the undead creature. For 1 minute (Concentration) you can slip under a door, through a keyhole or through any other tiny gap. Your equipment changes with you and you can move up to your full speed. You have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks in darkness or dim light and you are immune to nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. You can end the spell early with an action. If you return to normal in a space too small for you, such as a mouse hole or sewer pipe, you take 4d6 Force damage and are pushed to the nearest space within 50 feet that fits you. If it is farther than 50 feet, you take an extra 1d6 Force damage for every additional 10 feet traveled. **At Higher Levels.** You can affect one extra willing creature you touch for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Slow-Burn Fireball": "A bright streak shoots from your pointing finger to a point you choose within range and slowly ignites the air with phlogiston. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere there makes a Dexterity save and takes 4d6 Fire damage on a failure, or half on a success. Each creature that took damage takes the same damage again at the start of your next two turns, unless it uses an action to put out the flames on its clothes, hair and gear. Flammable objects in the area that nobody wears or carries also ignite. **At Higher Levels.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Smiting Arrow": "You need something directly tied to the intended target, such as a drop of blood, a strand of hair or a recently worn piece of clothing. The casting consumes it. You imbue a piece of ammunition for 24 hours. If it is used for a ranged attack against that specific target and hits, it deals an extra 6d10 Radiant damage and the target is Stunned for 1 round. A successful Constitution save halves the Radiant damage and avoids the Stunned condition. On a critical hit the target has Disadvantage on the save.",
"Snap the Leash": "Choose a beast you can see within 30 feet. If its Intelligence is 4 or higher, the spell fails. The beast makes a Wisdom save. On a failure you strip the shackles of domestication from its mind, and it forgets being broken or trained. Mounts refuse to be ridden and other animals lose all tricks and obedience they learned. Other memories remain, so an animal may still favor those who were kind to it and turn on those who hurt it. It can be tamed again, but training starts from zero. The spell works only in part on animal companions, familiars and paladin mounts. It removes their tricks, but the bond with their master is unaffected.",
"Snow Boulder": "A ball of snow forms 5 feet from you and rolls in a direction you point at 30 feet per move, growing as it goes. Concentration, up to 4 rounds. To roll it into a creature within 90 feet, you make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the creature makes a Dexterity save or is knocked Prone and takes damage based on the boulder's size. Hitting a creature does not stop the boulder or slow its growth while you keep concentrating. When the spell ends, the boulder stops. Damage by size: Small 1d6, Medium 2d6, Large 4d6, Huge 6d6, all Bludgeoning.",
"Snow Fort": "You raise a simple fort of packed snow in an unoccupied space within 120 feet. It surrounds a 10-foot area with sloping walls 4 feet high. It gives half cover (+2 AC) against ranged and melee attacks from outside. The walls have AC 12 and 30 hit points per side, are immune to Cold, Necrotic, Poison and Psychic damage, and are vulnerable to Fire damage. You can repair a damaged wall by casting a spell that deals Cold damage on it, restoring points equal to the damage, up to 30. The spell also makes a dozen snowballs that can be thrown (range 20/60) and deal 1d4 Bludgeoning plus 1d4 Cold damage on a hit.",
"Snowy Coat": "You alter a creature's appearance so that it has Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to hide in snowy terrain. The target can also use a bonus action to turn invisible in snowy terrain for 1 minute. The invisibility ends after the minute or when the creature attacks or casts a spell. Concentration, up to 1 hour. **At Higher Levels.** You can target one extra creature for each slot level above 1st.",
"Solitary Fireball": "A bright streak flashes from your pointing finger to a point you choose within range, where it blooms with a low roar and engulfs a single creature in fire. The creature takes 6d6 Fire damage, or half on a successful Dexterity save. Flammable objects nearby do not catch fire. **At Higher Levels.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Song of the Forest": "You can cast this spell only as a ritual, taking 10 minutes. You tune your senses to nature and hear every sound within 60 feet, such as wind in the branches, falling leaves, grazing deer and trickling streams. You can clearly picture each source. You gain tremorsense out to 10 feet and Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing. Silent or magically silenced creatures are not detected. The spell works only in natural places and fails underground, in a city, or in a building that cuts you off from nature, at the GM's discretion. Concentration, up to 10 minutes. **Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, you also gain blindsight out to 30 feet.",
"Soothing Chant": "You intone a lulling drone for 1 minute (Concentration). At the start of its turn, each creature that can hear you makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is Charmed. A Charmed creature can still act against your allies, and if it uses area attacks it aims them to avoid you. On a success it acts normally but must save again each round while you chant and it can hear you. As a bonus action on your turn you can name up to six other creatures that the Charmed creatures will not attack. The effect ends early if you or a named creature takes a hostile action against a Charmed creature or in its presence. A creature that you attack or target with a harmful spell, or that sees you do so to another Charmed creature, is freed from the spell and can act against you and your named creatures.",
"Soothing Incandescence": "A soft white glow spreads from a point above your head, filling a 30-foot radius with bright light around where you stand for 1 hour (Concentration). The light stays fixed in place if you move. Any creature in the area other than a fiend or undead regains 1 hit point at the start of each of its turns inside the light. Each fiend or undead in the area takes 2d4 Radiant damage at the start of each of its turns.",
"Soothsayer's Shield": "As a reaction when an enemy's attack hits you, you gain a +4 bonus to AC until the start of your next turn, including against the triggering attack.",
"Soul Borrowing": "You touch a creature and gain one of its senses, movement modes and speeds, feats, languages, immunities or other nonmagical abilities for 1 minute. The target keeps using the borrowed ability too. An unwilling target avoids the effect with a successful Constitution save. The target may be alive or dead for no more than 1 minute, and a corpse automatically fails the save. You can hold only one borrowed ability at a time. **At Higher Levels.** With a slot of 5th level or higher, the duration becomes 1 hour and the target loses the stolen ability while the spell lasts.",
"Soul of the Machine": "One willing creature you touch becomes immune to mind-altering effects and Psychic damage for 1 hour (Concentration).",
"Souleater": "You fill a weapon you touch with a hunger for life force for 1 hour (Concentration). It sheds dim light in a 30-foot radius, and weapon attacks with it deal an extra 2d8 Necrotic damage on a hit. If it is not already magical, it becomes a magic weapon with a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. As a bonus action you can end the spell to make the weapon release a burst of radiance. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 2d8 Necrotic damage and you regain half that many hit points. On a success it takes half damage and you regain nothing.",
"Speak with Inanimate Object": "You awaken the spirit inside an inanimate object such as a rock, a sign or a table, and can ask it up to three yes-or-no questions within 10 minutes. The spirit is indifferent to you unless you have harmed or helped it. It can tell you about its surroundings and what it has observed with its limited senses, and can act as a spy for you in some cases. The spell ends when the time runs out or after three answers.",
"Spectral Herd": "You summon a spectral herd of ponies to drag away a Large or smaller creature you can see within 30 feet. The target makes a Dexterity save. On a failure a spectral rope wraps around it, it falls Prone and is Restrained, and it is pulled 60 feet in a direction you choose behind the galloping herd. It takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage from being dragged. While it stays Restrained, it is dragged another 60 feet and takes another 3d6 Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of your turns. The herd keeps running in the chosen direction for 1 minute. You cannot change the direction once chosen, but the ponies swerve around impassable obstacles. They ignore difficult terrain and are immune to damage. The target can use its action to make a Strength or Dexterity check against your spell save DC to escape. The rope cannot be cut. **At Higher Levels.** You can target one extra creature for each slot level above 4th.",
"Sphere of Order": "You surround yourself with the perfect order of clockwork, affecting a 30-foot area around you. Chaotic creatures that start their turn in the area or enter it on their turn take 5d8 Psychic damage. The damage is 8d8 for Chaotic aberrations, celestials, elementals and fiends. A successful Wisdom save halves the damage, but Chaotic creatures, the only ones affected, make the save with Disadvantage.",
"Spin": "You pick a creature you can see within 60 feet and order it to spin. It resists with a successful Wisdom save. On a failure it spins in place for up to 1 minute. A spinning creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that has spun for 1 round or longer becomes dizzy and has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until 1 round after it stops spinning.",
"Spinning Axes": "Axes of luminous force burst out from you and strike every creature within 10 feet. Each takes 5d8 Force damage, or half on a successful Dexterity save. A damaged creature that is not undead or a construct begins to bleed. A bleeding creature takes 2d6 Necrotic damage at the end of each of its turns for 1 minute. A creature can stop the bleeding for itself or another by using an action to pass a Wisdom (Medicine) check against your spell save DC, or by receiving any magical healing. **At Higher Levels.** The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 4th.",
"Spire of Stone": "A spire of rock bursts from the ground, floor or other surface under your feet. It is as wide as your space and lifts you up to 20 feet. When it appears, a creature within 5 feet of you makes a Dexterity save or falls Prone. As a bonus action on your turn you can raise or lower the spire by up to 20 feet, to a maximum height of 40 feet. If you step off, it collapses at once. When it vanishes, the surface it came from is unharmed. You can raise a new spire as a bonus action while the spell lasts. Concentration, up to 10 minutes.",
"Spiteful Weapon": "Target a creature, an attacker that wounded it within the last 24 hours, and the melee weapon that caused the wound. All three must be within 25 feet when you cast. For up to 5 rounds (Concentration), whenever the attacker takes damage while holding that weapon, the target makes a Charisma save. On a failure the target takes the same amount and type of damage, or half on a success. The attacker can turn the weapon on itself to hurt the target with the same damage. A self-inflicted wound hits automatically but the damage is still rolled. Once linked, the connection holds regardless of range as long as all three stay on the same plane. The spell ends at once if the attacker receives any healing. **At Higher Levels.** With a slot of 5th level or higher, the target has Disadvantage on its Charisma saves.",
"Spur Mount": "As a bonus action you urge a mount you touch to a burst of speed. Until the end of your next turn, you can direct it to take the Dash or Disengage action as a bonus action. The spell does nothing to a creature you are not riding.",
}
